Two components are covered only by upstream's later notice. Their paragraphs are
reproduced here because the corresponding code is in this tree:

  * The QS Bar style at
    src/tenkai_core/shell/quickshell/shell/modules/bar/barstyles/qsbar/ is a port
    of Quickshell Rise by HANCORE-linux
    (https://github.com/HANCORE-linux/quickshell-dots). It is a modified
    version: Ryoku keeps Rise's island, full, fit, dock and notch forms, widgets,
    pop-up panels, settings panel and draggable editing, while replacing its
    Omarchy data and command integrations with Ryoku's wallpaper palette, neutral
    window-manager and host-service seams, package updates, wallpaper, media,
    audio, power and capture paths. Ryoku also rebrands the shell, merges its two
    runtime variants into one bar, and adds Ryoku settings and per-display
    controls. Quickshell Rise is released under the MIT License; that license is
    compatible with Ryoku's GPL-3 distribution, and the upstream license ships
    unchanged beside the port.

  * The Stage Editor (src/tenkai_core/shell/quickshell/shell/modules/stage/) is
    based on the Edit Mode of ii-p3drovfx by P3DROVFX and contributors
    (https://github.com/P3DROVFX/ii-p3drovfx), which builds on ii-vynx by
    vaguesyntax (https://github.com/vaguesyntax/ii-vynx) and end-4's
    illogical-impulse (https://github.com/end-4/dots-hyprland). It is a modified
    version: Ryoku runs it over its own desktop, widgets, wallpaper, visualizer
    and depth services, gives it the Ryoku look, and leaves out its lock screen,
    bar and dock editing. ii-p3drovfx is released under the GNU General Public
    License version 3; the ported portions keep that license, compatible with
    Ryoku's GPL-3.

  * The built-in desktop sounds under src/tenkai_core/shell/ipc/assets/ come from
